FACT good_land.the_way_of_forty_years(the_humbling) = ("the humbling (8:2-3, 8:16) — 'to humble you … he humbled you and let you hunger': the verb's seven Deuteronomy seats; the Day's affliction is HUNGER by the verbal analogy with 8:3 (Yoma 74b:11) — the analogy guarded twice: the public's affliction from the public's, God's hand from God's hand (74b:12-13); Onkelos 'afflict'", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 8:2-3, 8:16 — "to HUMBLE you … and he HUMBLED you and let you hunger" — the verb\'s seven Deuteronomy seats [(\'Deut 8:2\', \'ענתך\'), (\'Deut 8:3\', \'ויענך\'), (\'Deut 8:16\', \'ענתך\'), (\'Deut 21:14\', \'עניתה\'), (\'Deut 22:24\', \'ענה\'), (\'Deut 22:29\', \'ענה\'), (\'Deut 26:6\', \'ויענונו\')] (8:2, 3, 16; the seduced and the ravished; 26:6 the Egyptians\' "afflicted us"); the narrative verbs of the chapter [\'ויענך\', \'וירעבך\', \'ויאכלך\']'), ('MOVE', "Yoma 74b:11-13 (opened whole); Ketubot 47b:11 — the Day's affliction is HUNGER by the verbal analogy with 8:3 (the school of R. Yishmael) — guarded twice: not from Laban's daughters (the PUBLIC's affliction from the public's), not from Egypt's affliction (26:7 — BY THE HAND OF GOD from God's hand): the shelf reads 8:3's hunger as God's act on the whole people; 'onata' sustenance from 8:3 (R. Elazar)")])
