2 shared — the hunger God\'s act, the murmuring\'s occasion made the humbling\'s means) and 8:16 EXPANDED (13 against 8:3\'s 28, 3 shared — "to do you good in your end")'), ('DATA', 'manna_provided on Israel STANDS — a reference, no second write (CU5)')])
FACT good_land.the_way_of_forty_years(not_by_bread_alone) = ("not by bread alone (8:3) — 'but by everything that proceeds from the mouth of the LORD': a teaching, not an act (the Sifrei 48:10 — the exposition; Onkelos 'the Word of the LORD'); the daily manna's reason on the shelf — everyone's heart to Heaven every day (Yoma 76a:2-3); 18:5's living by CALL: a DATA row, no write", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 8:3 — "that he might make you know that NOT BY BREAD ALONE does man live, but by EVERYTHING THAT PROCEEDS FROM THE MOUTH OF THE LORD does man live" — [\'Deut 8:3\'] and [\'Deut 8:3\'] one seat each; "man shall live" [\'Deut 8:3\', \'Eccl 11:8\']; "the mouth of the LORD" 25 Torah seats; "and live by them" [\'Ezek 20:11\', \'Ezek 20:13\', \'Ezek 20:21\', \'Lev 18:5\'] (the sanctions\' living)'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 48:10 (read whole at the reading); Yoma 74b:14, 76a:2-3 (opened whole); cold_run_sanctions (CALL) — SA.frame(live_by_them, private) = transgress_and_live — 'not by bread alone' = the exposition; 'everything that proceeds' = the laws and the homilies (R. Shimon ben Menasya); the daily manna's reason — the king's one son, 'everyone's heart to their Father in Heaven every day'; Leviticus 18:5's 'live by them, not die by them' the living's kin"), ('DATA', 'the row not_by_bread_alone: {\'the_teaching\': "\'not by bread alone does man live, but by everything that proceeds from the mouth of the LORD does man live\' (8:3) — a TEACHING, not an act: no write", \'the_sifrei\': "48:10 (read whole at the reading): \'not by bread alone\' = the exposition; \'everything that proceeds from the mouth of the LORD\' = the laws and the homilies (R. Shimon ben Menasya)", \'the_shelf\': "Yoma 74b:14 — the affliction IN the manna (R. Ami / R. Asi: no bread in the basket for tomorrow / the food not seen as it tastes); 76a:2-3 — the daily manna\'s reason: the king\'s one son, \'everyone\'s heart to their Father in Heaven every day\' (8:3\'s \'to humble you\' and 8:16\'s \'to test you\' in the shelf\'s words); Ketubot 47b \'onata\' sustenance from 8:3", \'onkelos\': "\'not by bread alone is man SUSTAINED, but by everything that PROCEEDS FROM THE WORD (the Memra) OF THE LORD\' — the Memra (the Word) at 8:3 and 8:20, the chapter\'s two", \'the_living\': "\'man shall live\' 8:3 and Ecclesiastes 11:8; \'and live by them\' Leviticus 18:5 (sanctions.frame(\'live_by_them\') by CALL — \'live by them, not die by them\')"}')])
FACT good_land.the_way_of_forty_years(the_garment_and_the_foot) = ("the garment and the foot (8:4) — a STATE over forty years told only here (29:4 the plural garments; Nehemiah 9:21 the only other 'did not swell'; Onkelos 'your shoes did not go bare'): no line on the tape, no entry on any ledger (the scan empty) — the readback's FIFTH FORM, graded SUPPLIED with NO retrograde write (a condition has no day); cited by no row on the shelf", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 8:4 — "YOUR GARMENT DID NOT WEAR OUT upon you, nor did YOUR FOOT SWELL, these forty years" — "your garment did not wear out" [\'Deut 8:4\', \'Neh 9:21\'] (29:4 the plural garments); "did not swell" the verb\'s TWO Bible seats [(\'Deut 8:4\', \'בצקה\'), (\'Neh 9:21\', \'בצקו\')]; a STATE over [40] years, the negatives the past (the prohibition form nowhere here [(\'בלתה\', \'HVqp3fs\'), (\'בצקה\', \'HVqp3fs\')])'), ('DATA', "THE READBACK'S FIFTH FORM — THE RETELLING OF A STATE: no line on the tape (an act has a day; a forty-year condition has none), NO ENTRY on any ledger (the one database's run_ledger scanned for a garment, clothing, a shoe or a swelling on israel_people: []; CU7 the same scan on the running world) — graded SUPPLIED with NO retrograde write (the design's decision, open to the owner); the row the_garment_and_the_foot: 'your garment did not wear out upon you, nor did your foot swell, these forty years' (8:4) — a CONDITION over [40] years, told only here (29:4 'your clothes did not wear out … your shoe upon your foot' the plural, in Moses' last speech; Nehemiah 9:21 'their clothes did not wear out and their feet did not swell' the only other 'did not swell')"), ('MOVE', "Onkelos 8:4 (read whole at the reading); the docket's scan — 'your shoes did not go bare' — the Aramaic reads the shoe where the Hebrew reads the foot (8:4, 29:4); NO ROW ON THE SHELF cites 8:4 (the scan: the ten verses cited by no one)")])
FACT good_land.the_way_of_forty_years(the_discipline) = ("the discipline (8:5) — 'as a man disciplines his son, so the LORD your God disciplines you': 1:31's carrying made the discipline (OS by CALL — the readback row VARIANT); the Land acquired through suffering, the second of three gifts (Berakhot 5a:20-22; the afflictions of love 5a:10); Onkelos 'teaches'", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 8:5 — "and you shall know with your heart that AS A MAN DISCIPLINES HIS SON, so the LORD your God disciplines you" — [\'Deut 8:5\'] one seat; "as a man … his son" [\'2Kgs 23:10\', \'Deut 1:31\', \'Deut 8:5\'] (1:31 the carrying, 2 Kings 23:10 Molech); the discipline-lemma\'s Torah seats [\'Deut 4:36\', \'Deut 8:5\', \'Deut 8:5\', \'Deut 21:18\', \'Deut 22:18\', \'Lev 26:18\', \'Lev 26:23\', \'Lev 26:28\']; "with your heart" [\'Deut 15:9\', \'Deut 8:5\']'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_opening_speech (CALL) — OS.the_spies_read_back(the_carrying) = the carrying (1:31) — as a man carries his son: Exodus 19:4'; Berakhot 5a:10, 5a:20-22 (opened whole); the Sifrei 32:10-15 (credited) — 1:31's 'as a man carries his son' made the discipline — the two seats of the form; the afflictions of love ('as a father the son in whom he delights', Proverbs 3:12); THE LAND ACQUIRED THROUGH SUFFERING — the second of R. Shimon ben Yochai's three gifts: 'as a man rebukes his son' (8:5) and thereafter 'a good land' (8:7)"), ('DATA', "the readback row 8:5 VARIANT — computed 12 tokens against 1:31's 21, 3 shared (carried → disciplined)")])
FACT good_land.the_way_of_forty_years(keep_walk_fear) = ("keep, walk, fear (8:6) — 'to walk in his ways' 8:6, 30:16 and Solomon's charge; 'to fear him' the one seat; 10:12's 'what does the LORD your God ask of you' forward; Onkelos supplies 'right before him': a DATA note, no write", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 8:6 — "and you shall keep the commandments of the LORD your God, to walk in his ways and to fear him" — "to walk in his ways" [\'1Kgs 2:3\', \'Deut 30:16\', \'Deut 8:6\']; "in ALL his ways" [\'1Kgs 8:58\', \'Deut 10:12\', \'Deut 11:22\']; "and to fear him" [\'Deut 8:6\'] one seat; "to fear the LORD" in the book [\'Deut 10:12\', \'Deut 14:23\', \'Deut 17:19\', \'Deut 31:13\', \'Deut 6:24\']'), ('DATA', "10:12's 'what does the LORD your God ask of you' forward; Onkelos supplies 'the ways that are RIGHT BEFORE HIM' (8:6, 19:9, 26:17, 28:9, 30:16 — the five seats of the supplement)")])
FACT good_land.the_way_of_forty_years(the_messianic_forty) = ("the messianic forty (8:3) — R. Eliezer: the days of the Messiah forty years, 'afflicted' at 8:3 and Psalm 90:15 a verbal analogy (Sanhedrin 99a): the exam's row on the two [40]s, a DATA note", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 8:3 — "and he afflicted you" — the verb at 8:3 (ויענך) and Psalm 90:15 "according to the days you afflicted us"'), ('MOVE', "Sanhedrin 99a:5 (opened whole) — R. Eliezer: the days of the Messiah FORTY YEARS — 'afflicted' here (8:3, the forty-year sojourn) and 'afflicted' there (Psalm 90:15 'the years we saw evil'): a verbal analogy on the verb")])
