CELL blessing_and_curse.the_land_watered_by_heaven: asks 7 ['all_the_commandment', 'the_oath_to_the_fathers', 'not_like_egypt', 'drinks_by_the_rain_of_heaven', 'the_land_watered_first', 'the_eyes_from_the_years_beginning', 'the_decree_and_the_season'] | keys 0 [] | matching 'rain|dew|former|latter|season|days|prolong|eyes': ['drinks_by_the_rain_of_heaven', 'the_eyes_from_the_years_beginning', 'the_decree_and_the_season']
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_land_watered_by_heaven(drinks_by_the_rain_of_heaven) = ("drinks by the rain of heaven (11:11) — the one seat; THE SOURCE OF RAIN A DISPUTE on the shelf (R. Eliezer the ocean sweetened in the clouds; R. Yehoshua the upper waters — 11:11 his verse: Ta'anit 9b:10-11); no water channels in the Land (Bava Batra 19a:18): the readback row EXPANDED by CALL (GL.the_good_land); the digger of channels accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:11 — "but the land which you are crossing over to possess is a land of hills and valleys; BY THE RAIN OF HEAVEN IT DRINKS WATER" — "a land of hills and valleys" the one seat [\'Deut 11:11\'] (8:7 "in the valley and in the hill" the pair reversed [\'Deut 8:7\']); "by the rain of heaven it drinks water" the one seat [\'Deut 11:11\']; "rain" the lemma\'s Torah seats [(\'Deut 11:11\', \'למטר\'), (\'Deut 11:14\', \'מטר\'), (\'Deut 11:17\', \'מטר\'), (\'Deut 28:12\', \'מטר\'), (\'Deut 28:24\', \'מטר\'), (\'Deut 32:2\', \'כמטר\'), (\'Exod 9:33\', \'ומטר\'), (\'Exod 9:34\', \'המטר\')]; "drinks water" the two seats [\'1Kgs 13:9\', \'Deut 11:11\'] (1 Kings 13:9 the man of God\'s); the shared run with 8:7 2'), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 9b:10-11, 9b:14-16, 10a:4-7 (read whole at the docket); Bava Batra 19a:18 — THE SOURCE OF RAIN A DISPUTE — R. Eliezer: the whole world drinks from the ocean's waters, sweetened in the clouds (Genesis 2:6's mist; 'darkness of waters' / 'gathering of waters' the two verses' one letter); R. YEHOSHUA: FROM THE UPPER WATERS — 'BY THE RAIN OF HEAVEN IT DRINKS WATER' (11:11) HIS VERSE, the clouds rising to receive it (Job 36:27); no water channels needed in the Land — the mishna's plow distanced for seeds, not for channels (Bava Batra 19a:18)"), ('MOVE', "cold_run_good_land (CALL) — GL.the_good_land(the_good_land) = the good land (8:7, 8:10) — twelve seats of 'a good land', t — 8:7-10's praise of the land (the waters, the seven species) — 11:11's praise its kin: the readback row EXPANDED by CALL"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 11:11 — EXPANDED by CALL (GL.the_good_land); THE SOURCE OF RAIN a parameter with two arms (the ocean / the upper waters — 11:11 R. Yehoshua\'s verse) — a DATA row the design did not predict; the exam\'s person the one who digs water channels in the Land — no need (19a:18): accepted; Onkelos "למטר שמיא שתיא מיא" (by the rain of the heavens it drinks water)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_land_watered_by_heaven(the_eyes_from_the_years_beginning) = ("the eyes from the year's beginning (11:12) — the one seat, 'from the beginning' defective (the one token): THE YEAR JUDGED AT ITS HEAD (Rosh Hashanah 8a:16 — the New Year for years is for judgment; 16b:12 the three books; 16b:3 the poor year made rich, the do-not-read reading named); 11:12's 'year' the analogy's anchor for the sabbatical and the planting (8b:6, 9b:11 — I2), refused for the months (7a:18)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:12 — "the eyes of the LORD your God are always on it, FROM THE BEGINNING OF THE YEAR TO THE END OF THE YEAR" — the phrase the one seat [\'Deut 11:12\']; "from the beginning" DEFECTIVE (without the alef) the ONE token [\'Deut 11:12\'] against the lemma\'s twenty-eight full "beginning"s and four "from the beginning"s; the shared run with Psalm 34:16 2, Zechariah 4:10 2'), ('MOVE', "Rosh Hashanah 8a:16, 16b:3, 16b:12, 8b:6, 9b:11, 7a:18 (read whole at the docket); Berakhot 55a:9 — THE YEAR JUDGED AT ITS HEAD — Rav Nachman bar Yitzchak: the first of Tishri the New Year for years is FOR JUDGMENT, 'from the beginning of the year to its end' (8a:16 — from the beginning what will be at the end is judged); THREE BOOKS opened at Rosh Hashanah (16b:12 — R. Kruspedai in R. Yochanan's name: the wholly righteous, the wholly wicked, the middling to Yom Kippur); R. Yitzchak: A YEAR POOR AT ITS HEAD IS MADE RICH AT ITS END — 'from the beginning' written defectively read 'poverty' (16b:3 — the do-not-read reading NAMED, no code); 'year' / 'year' with 11:12 the verbal analogy (I2 — checked in MIDDOT.md) for the sabbatical (8b:6) and the planting (9b:11), REFUSED for the months' count (7a:18); a good year needs mercy (Berakhot 55a:9)"), ('DATA', '11:12\'s "year" the calendar\'s anchor by analogy (Rosh Hashanah 8b:6, 9b:11) — calendar by the registry\'s own rows; the defective spelling the store\'s (the reading\'s find) — a DATA row; Onkelos "מריש שתא ועד סוף שתא" (from the beginning of the year to the end of the year)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_land_watered_by_heaven(the_decree_and_the_season) = ("the decree and the season (11:12, 11:14) — Rosh Hashanah 17b:11-13: the rain decreed at the head of the year cannot be added to or reduced, but falls IN SEASON on the land that needs it for good, OUT OF SEASON on forests and deserts for bad — 'in its season' THE FREE VARIABLE AFTER THE DECREE, rain_in_its_season's value; the one who asks to add rain after the decree accepted against", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:12, 11:14 — "the eyes of the LORD your God are always on it" (11:12) — "I will give the rain of your land IN ITS SEASON" (11:14) — "in its season" [\'Deut 11:14\']; "the rain of your land" [\'Deut 11:14\'] (28:12 "to give the rain of your land in its season" the pair forward [\'Deut 28:12\'])'), ('MOVE', "Rosh Hashanah 17b:11-13 (read whole at the docket) — THE DECREE FIXED AT THE HEAD OF THE YEAR, THE DISTRIBUTION FREE — the baraita on 11:12: God's providence over the Land for good and for bad. FOR GOOD: wholly wicked at Rosh Hashanah, meager rain decreed, then they repented — to ADD rain is impossible, the decree is issued; rather He brings the sparse rain AT THE RIGHT TIMES on the land that needs it (fields, vineyards, gardens), as good as much. FOR BAD (17b:12): wholly righteous at Rosh Hashanah, much rain decreed, then they sinned — to REDUCE is impossible; He brings it OUT OF SEASON on forests and deserts. Why not tear the sentence for good? — the same result by time and place without rescinding (17b:13): 'IN ITS SEASON' (11:14) THE FREE VARIABLE AFTER THE DECREE — rain_in_its_season's VALUE made precise; Ta'anit 8b:5-6 the mountains or the fields, the trees or the seeds or the cisterns"), ('DATA', "THE EFFECT rain_in_its_season's value — the amount decreed at the year's head (11:12), the season and the place free (11:14): a DATA row the design did not predict (the docket's crown); the exam's person the one who asks to add rain after the decree — accepted against (the time and the place answer him)")])
CELL blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph: asks 18 ['if_you_hearken', 'the_yoke_of_the_commandments', 'the_rain_in_its_season', 'the_early_and_the_late', 'the_rains_dates', 'the_prayer_from_the_clause', 'the_cattle_first', 'take_heed_lest', 'the_heavens_shut', 'the_shuttings_threshold', 'the_shuttings_causes', 'perish_quickly', 'these_my_words', 'the_frontlets_plural', 'teach_your_sons', 'the_doorposts_plural', 'the_days_multiplied', 'the_class_rule'] | keys 0 [] | matching 'days|prolong|children|teach|heaven|shut|rain': ['the_rain_in_its_season', 'the_rains_dates', 'the_heavens_shut', 'the_shuttings_threshold', 'the_shuttings_causes', 'teach_your_sons', 'the_days_multiplied']
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_rain_in_its_season) = ("the rain in its season (11:14) — Leviticus 26:4's 'I will give your rains in their season' (TC.covenant by CALL — covenant_upheld the cell's; no line on the tape) with THE TWO NAMED RAINS ADDED (the one seat) and 7:13's grain, wine and oil (SN by CALL): the readback row VARIANT; THE WRITE rain_in_its_season — a conditional HEAVEN entry on Israel, the tape's first entry naming the rain (the hole filled)", ['rain_in_its_season'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:14 — "AND I WILL GIVE THE RAIN OF YOUR LAND IN ITS SEASON, the early rain and the late rain, and you shall gather your grain, your wine and your oil" — the clause the one seat [\'Deut 11:14\']; "and I will give" in God\'s mouth inside Moses\' speech the book\'s three [\'Deut 11:14\', \'Deut 11:15\', \'Deut 18:18\'] (11:14, 11:15, 18:18); "the early rain and the late rain" THE ONE SEAT [\'Deut 11:14\']; the shared run with Leviticus 26:4 1 (ONE token — "in its season" the retelling\'s own word: 26:4\'s "your rains in their season" [\'ונתתי\', \'גשמיכם\', \'בעתם\']), with 7:13 3'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_tochacha (CALL) — TC.covenant(True, True, True) = blessing / fx ['covenant_upheld']; cold_run_seven_nations (CALL) — SN.because_you_hear(the_blessing_list) = the blessing's list (7:13) — 23:25's bread and water expande — LEVITICUS 26:3-5 — 'if you walk in My statutes … I will give your rains in their season, and the land shall give its produce' (the covenant cell's blessing entry, covenant_upheld its effect; NO LINE ON THE TAPE — the tochacha's kinds exam cases: the recon); 7:13's grain, wine and oil (the blessing's list): THE TWO NAMED RAINS ADDED to Leviticus's clause — the readback row 11:14 VARIANT by CALL; NO EFFECT ANYWHERE NAMED THE RAIN before this sitting (the vocabulary ['rain_in_its_season', 'restraint_failed', 'speech_restrained']; the one database on Israel []): THE HOLE"), ('DATA', 'THE WRITE rain_in_its_season — a conditional HEAVEN entry on israel_people (blessings_for_hearing\'s form — 7:12\'s; treasured_people\'s, Exodus 19:5) on the line second_paragraph_declared: its value the decree fixed at the year\'s head and its season free (Rosh Hashanah 17b:11-13); the readback row 11:14 VARIANT; Onkelos "ואתין מטר ארעכון בעדניה בכיר ולקיש" (and I will give the rain of your land in its season, early and late)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_rains_dates) = ("the rain's dates (11:14) — a PARAMETER, every value from a row: the mention from the feast's last day to Passover's first (Ta'anit 2a:1-3), the request from the seventh of Marcheshvan (Rabban Gamliel, the ruling — 10a:11-12), sixty days abroad (Chananya — 10a:12, 10a:15), the fasts from the seventeenth and from Kislev's New Moon (10a:16): the one who requests rain at the feast accepted against", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:14 — "in its season" — the season NAMED BY THE SHELF, never a constant in the code: the parameter rain_dates\' keys [\'early_rain\', \'fasts_community\', \'fasts_individuals\', \'late_rain\', \'mention_from\', \'mention_to\', \'request_from_diaspora\', \'request_from_land\']'), ('MOVE', "Mishnah Ta'anit 1:1-5 through the Gemara (Ta'anit 2a:1-3, 10a:11-16 — read whole at the docket; the export lacks the Mishnah's own file) — THE MENTION from the feast's last day (R. Yehoshua — the eighth day of assembly; R. Eliezer from the first festival day; rain during the feast a curse's sign — 2a:1-2) to Passover's first day (R. Yehuda's prayer leaders — 2a:3); THE REQUEST only near the season (2a:3) — from the third of Marcheshvan, or THE SEVENTH (Rabban Gamliel — fifteen days after the feast for the last pilgrim to reach the Euphrates: THE HALAKHA (THE RULING), 10a:11-12), in the diaspora SIXTY DAYS into the season (Chananya — the halakha (the ruling), 10a:12; the sixtieth day counted after, Rav Pappa 10a:15); THE FASTS — the seventeenth of Marcheshvan without rain, individuals three fasts (the Sages, Monday-Thursday-Monday, 10a:16-19); the New Moon of Kislev, the court decrees three on the community (10a:16)"), ('DATA', "rain_dates written into calendar_parameters.yaml with the docket's rows (the sojourn_start form — exercised by this runner's DATA, no timer, no clock walk): request_from_land 'the seventh of Marcheshvan (Rabban Gamliel — the halakha (th'; the exam's person the one who requests rain at the feast — accepted against (a curse's sign, 2a:2)")])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_heavens_shut) = ("the heavens shut (11:17) — Leviticus 26:19-20's iron heavens (TC.cascade(1) by CALL — the second block, no line on the tape) told as the shutting: the readback row VARIANT; THE WRITE heavens_shut_for_turning — a conditional HEAVEN entry on Israel, its value THE CLOUDS AND THE WINDS WITHHELD, not rain alone (Ta'anit 3b:6)", ['heavens_shut_for_turning'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:17 — "and the anger of the LORD be kindled against you, and HE SHUT UP THE HEAVENS AND THERE BE NO RAIN, and the ground not give its produce, and you perish quickly from off the good land which the LORD gives you" — "and He shut up the heavens" the one seat [\'Deut 11:17\'] (the lemma\'s Torah seats [(\'Deut 11:17\', \'ועצר\'), (\'Deut 32:36\', \'עצור\'), (\'Gen 16:2\', \'עצרני\'), (\'Gen 20:18\', \'עצר\'), (\'Gen 20:18\', \'עצר\'), (\'Num 17:13\', \'ותעצר\'), (\'Num 17:15\', \'נעצרה\'), (\'Num 25:8\', \'ותעצר\')]); "and the anger of the LORD be kindled against you" the three seats [\'Deut 11:17\', \'Deut 7:4\', \'Josh 23:16\'] (Joshua 23:16 the run\'s receipt); "the ground not give its produce" against Leviticus 26:4\'s "the land shall give its produce" [\'Lev 26:4\'] and 26:20\'s "your land shall not give its produce" [\'Lev 26:20\']; the shared run with Leviticus 26:20 5, Joshua 23:16 11'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_tochacha (CALL) — TC.cascade(1) stage 2, span (19, 20), fx ['chastised_sevenfold']; TC.covenant(False, False, False) = curse_entry — LEVITICUS 26:19-20 — 'I will make your heaven as iron and your earth as brass; your strength shall be spent in vain, your land shall not give its produce' (the cascade's SECOND BLOCK, the gate at 26:18 — chastised_sevenfold; NO LINE ON THE TAPE): the retelling's 'He shut up the heavens' the iron heaven's own word — the readback row 11:17 VARIANT by CALL"), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 3b:6 (read whole at the docket) — THE SHUTTING'S VALUE — Rav Yosef's baraita: 'and He will shut up the heavens' (11:17) — from THE CLOUDS AND FROM THE WINDS; do you say from the clouds and the winds, or only no rain? when the verse says 'so that there will be no rain', rain is already said — 'shut up the heavens' must mean FROM THE CLOUDS AND THE WINDS: the effect's value, not rain alone"), ('DATA', 'THE WRITE heavens_shut_for_turning — a conditional HEAVEN entry on israel_people on the line second_paragraph_declared: its value the clouds and the winds withheld (Ta\'anit 3b:6 — a DATA row the design did not predict); the readback row 11:17 VARIANT; Onkelos "ויחוד ית שמיא ולא יהי מטרא" (and He will shut the heavens and there will be no rain)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_shuttings_threshold) = ("the shutting's threshold (11:17) — rains that seal a barrel's mouth with their mud are not 'shut' (Rav Chisda, Ta'anit 6b:8; the first rainfall a handbreadth, R. Abbahu); the shutting verb the wombs' — closing, birth and remembering said of a woman and of rain (Reish Lakish in bar Kappara's name, 8a:18, 8b:1-3; the Sifrei 306:6)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:17 — "He shut up the heavens and there be no rain" — the shutting-lemma\'s Bible seats beside the wombs\' [(\'1Chr 12:1\', \'עצור\'), (\'1Chr 21:22\', \'ותעצר\'), (\'1Chr 29:14\', \'נעצר\'), (\'1Kgs 8:35\', \'בהעצר\'), (\'1Kgs 14:10\', \'עצור\'), (\'1Kgs 18:44\', \'יעצרכה\'), (\'1Kgs 21:21\', \'ועצור\'), (\'1Sam 9:17\', \'יעצר\')] (Genesis 20:18 "the LORD had fast closed up all the wombs")'), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 6b:8; 8a:18, 8b:1-3 (read whole at the docket) — THE THRESHOLD — R. Abbahu: the first rainfall saturates the ground a handbreadth, the second seals a barrel's mouth with its mud; Rav Chisda: rains that seal a barrel's mouth with mud are NOT 'He will shut up the heavens and there will be no rain' (6b:8) — the shutting's measure; THE SHUTTING VERB THE WOMBS' — Reish Lakish: the heavens closed from dew and rain like a woman in labor who cannot give birth; bar Kappara: 'closing' said of rains (11:17) and of a woman (Genesis 20:18), 'giving birth' of a woman (30:23) and of rain (Isaiah 55:10), 'remembering' of Sarah (21:1) and of the earth watered (Psalm 65:10): THREE ANALOGIES (8a:18, 8b:1-3) — the Sifrei 306:6's reading at its Bavli seat (the design's note confirmed)"), ('DATA', "the threshold a PARAMETER row (the barrel's mud) — a DATA row the design did not predict; the wombs' verb the reading's find confirmed at 8b:1 (credited to the Genesis triage, read whole here)")])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_shuttings_causes) = ("the shutting's causes (11:16-17) — the chapter's one cause (other gods) beside the shelf's many (the sentence of destruction from 11:17, the tithes, slander, the impudent, the neglect of Torah, robbery, no whisperers, false pledges — Ta'anit 7b:5-8a:8, 8b:16): a parameter with many arms; the remedy prayer and the pious; the fasts the run's response (10a:16): the community that fasts from Kislev's New Moon accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:16-17 — "lest your heart be deceived and you turn aside and serve other gods … and He shut up the heavens" — THE CHAPTER\'S OWN CAUSE the turning to other gods; "and you perish quickly from off the good land" [\'Deut 11:17\']'), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 7b:5-8a:8, 8a:14, 8b:16, 10a:16 (read whole at the docket) — THE CAUSES ON THE SHELF — Ze'iri from Dihavat: 'we learned it from here — He will shut up the heavens … and you perish quickly' (11:17 — the sentence of destruction, 7b:5); the tithes annulled (Rav Chisda, 7b:6); slander (7b:7); the impudent (7b:8); dereliction of Torah (7b:10-11); robbery (7b:12); no whisperers of prayer (8a:6); charity pledged in public and not given (8b:16); the faithful alone bring rain (8a:14): THE CAUSE A PARAMETER WITH MANY ARMS beside the chapter's one; THE REMEDY — prayer (7b:13, 7b:15), the generation's most pious (8a:8); THE RUN'S RESPONSE — the fasts from the seventeenth of Marcheshvan (individuals) and the New Moon of Kislev (the court, the community) — Mishnah Ta'anit 1:4-5 through 10a:16"), ('DATA', "the causes a DATA row (a parameter with many arms — the design did not predict); the exam's person the community that fasts from Kislev's New Moon — the court's decree holds: accepted; the remedy prayer")])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(teach_your_sons) = ("teach your sons (11:19) — 'and you shall teach them' (the piel) against 6:7's 'repeat them': HI.the_four_duties('teach_your_sons', 'daughters_exempt') by CALL — the readback row VARIANT; 'you shall teach them' read 'you yourselves' (Bava Batra 21a:2 — Yehoshua ben Gamla's schools for the fatherless): the father who leaves the teaching to the school accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:19 — "AND YOU SHALL TEACH THEM TO YOUR SONS, speaking of them when you sit in your house and walk on the way and lie down and rise up" — "and you shall teach them to your sons" the one seat [\'Deut 11:19\'] against 6:7\'s "and you shall repeat them to your sons" [\'Deut 6:7\'] (Onkelos\'s two verbs); "and you shall teach" the consecutive perfect\'s seats in the book [(\'Deut 5:1\', \'ולמדתם\'), (\'Deut 11:19\', \'ולמדתם\')]; the shared run with 6:7 7'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_hear_o_israel (CALL) — HI.the_four_duties(teach_your_sons) = teach your sons (6:7) — the father's duty to teach Torah, th; (daughters_exempt) = the daughters (6:7) — 'your sons', not your daughters: the d / fx ['exempt'] — the father's duty to teach Torah, the disciples 'sons' (the Sifrei 34:1; 46:1 'your sons and not your daughters' — Kiddushin 29b credited); Bava Batra 21a:2 (read whole at the docket): 'AND YOU SHALL TEACH THEM' read 'YOU YOURSELVES' shall teach — the do-not-read reading named, no code: the father the teacher; YEHOSHUA BEN GAMLA'S ORDINANCE — the fatherless learned nothing, so schools in every town (the run's institution); Berakhot 15b:27 the teaching complete (credited)"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 11:19 — VARIANT by CALL ("teach" the piel against 6:7\'s "repeat"); the exam\'s person the father who leaves the teaching to the school — the school for the fatherless, the father the teacher: accepted; Onkelos "ותלפון יתהון ית בניכון" (and you shall teach them to your sons)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_days_multiplied) = ("the days multiplied (11:21) — 'as the days of the heavens above the earth' the one seat; 6:2's three generations by CALL (HI.the_header): the readback row VARIANT; the resurrection from 'to give to them' (the Sifrei 47:2; Sanhedrin 90b:12), the messianic era's measure (99a:10), lengthened in the Land (Berakhot 8a:6), the adjacency's reach (Shabbat 32b:4 — E28)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:21 — "THAT YOUR DAYS AND THE DAYS OF YOUR SONS BE MULTIPLIED on the land which the LORD swore to your fathers TO GIVE TO THEM, AS THE DAYS OF THE HEAVENS ABOVE THE EARTH" — "that your days be multiplied" the one seat [\'Deut 11:21\']; "as the days of the heavens above the earth" the one seat [\'Deut 11:21\'] (Psalm 89:30 "as the days of heaven" [\'Ps 89:30\']); "which the LORD swore to your fathers to give to them" the two seats [\'Deut 11:21\', \'Deut 11:9\'] (11:9, 11:21); the shared run with 11:9 8'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_hear_o_israel (CALL) — HI.the_header(your_sons_son) = your son's son (6:2) — three generations in the fear; Exodus — 6:2's three generations in the fear: the readback row 11:21 VARIANT by CALL; THE RESURRECTION FROM 'TO THEM' — 'to give to them', not 'to you': the fathers rise to receive it (the Sifrei 47:2; Sanhedrin 90b:12 credited from the Devarim docket); the messianic era as long as from creation to now, 'as the days of the heavens' (Sanhedrin 99a:10); lengthened in the Land and not outside — R. Yochanan on the elders of Babylonia (Berakhot 8a:6); 'a blessing is different', many days AND years (Shabbat 105b:11); 'your sons' inclusive at the reward — daughters too (Bava Batra 110b:7); children die for the mezuzah's neglect or the study's — the adjacency's reach (Shabbat 32b:4, E28 — checked in MIDDOT.md)"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 11:21 — VARIANT by CALL (HI.the_header); the resurrection\'s seat "to them" a DATA row; the dead outside the Land (Ketubot 111a:16-21) the seat\'s edge; Onkelos "כיומי שמיא על ארעא" (as the days of the heavens above the earth)')])
