FACT second_tablets.the_stations_and_the_death(and_he_was_buried_there) = ("and he was buried there (10:6) — the Torah's one seat; Numbers 20:28-29 and 33:38-39 tell the death, the mourning and the age, never the burial: the tape's hole — SUPPLIED with the write buried on aaron (REUSED — the world's ninth), dated (40, 5, 1) by the retrograde marker at Deut 10:6", ['buried'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:6 — "AND HE WAS BURIED THERE" — the niphal wayyiqtol "and he was buried" with "there" the Torah\'s ONE SEAT [\'Deut 10:6\'] (the Bible\'s twelve); Numbers 20:28 tells the death on the mountain\'s top and the descent of Moses and Eleazar, 33:38-39 the date and the age ([1], [40, 5], [123]), 20:29 the thirty days\' mourning — NEVER THE BURIAL; the bury-lemma\'s Torah seats 35'), ('DATA', "THE T2 ROW — SUPPLIED WITH A WRITE: the one database scanned on aaron for the burial [] (no entry); the world's buried before this sitting ['abraham', 'deborah_the_nurse', 'isaac', 'jacob', 'miriam', 'rachel', 'sarah', 'the_lusters'] — Sarah, Abraham, Deborah, Rachel, Isaac, Jacob, the lusters, Miriam: AARON THE NINTH; the act aaron_buried (subject aaron; place the OPEN row's field) written ONCE at its own day by the RETROGRADE marker at Deut 10:6 — M['burial_told'] = M['aaron_death'] = (40, 5, 1) (reading_placed); THE WRITE buried — the STATUS REUSED (Genesis's and Miriam's effect; a reused effect is a second entry and moves an older count — 6b's lesson: no checkpoint literal counts 'buried', grepped at the design)"), ('MOVE', "Sotah 14a:4 (read whole at the docket) — 'AFTER THE LORD YOUR GOD YOU SHALL WALK' (13:5) — R. Chama bar Chanina: walk after His attributes — He clothed the naked (Genesis 3:21), visited the sick (18:1), comforted mourners (25:11), BURIED THE DEAD ('and He buried him in the valley', 34:6): the burial among the attributes — beside 10:6's PASSIVE burial (Moses' by God's hand, Aaron's by no named hand)")])
FACT second_tablets.the_stations_and_the_death(the_place_of_the_death) = ("the place of the death — Moserah in the retelling (10:6), Mount Hor on the tape (Num 20:28, 33:38): an OPEN row inside the burial line's field; the retreat of seven stations (Seder Olam Rabbah 9:2) already a parameter — chukat.DATA['moserah'] = journeys.DATA['the_deuteronomy_order'] = the_retreat_of_seven_stations (by CALL); no marker for the retreat", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:6 — "from Beeroth-bene-jaakan TO MOSERAH; THERE Aaron died" against Numbers 33:38 "and Aaron the priest went up to MOUNT HOR … and died there" and 20:28 — Moserah/Moseroth\'s five Bible seats [\'Deut 10:6\', \'Jer 27:2\', \'Jer 5:5\', \'Num 33:30\', \'Num 33:31\'] (Jeremiah\'s "bonds" the homograph at 5:5, 27:2); Mount Hor the tape\'s place (journeyed_to_mount_hor at 20:22, M[\'hor_arrival\'] = (40, 4, 1) — the arrival to the death 29 days)'), ('MOVE', "Seder Olam Rabbah 9:2 (READ WHOLE at the docket — the export's chapters under its empty key); cold_run_chukat (CALL) — CK.edom_and_hor(moserah) = Moserah — the retreat of seven stations after Arad's attack, the mourning renewed there (S — THE RETREAT OF SEVEN STATIONS — 'from where Aaron died they retreated seven stations until Moserah' (after the king of Arad came; the mourning renewed there — 'there Aaron died' said of the mourning's place): the shelf's reconciliation ALREADY A PARAMETER of the Numbers compile — chukat.DATA['moserah'] = the_retreat_of_seven_stations = journeys.DATA['the_deuteronomy_order'] = the_retreat_of_seven_stations"), ('MOVE', "cold_run_chukat (CALL) — CK.edom_and_hor(seder_olam_walk) = the fortieth year's walk: (40, 1, 1) the arrival, three months at Kadesh, Aaron's death, t — the fortieth year's walk on the shelf: the arrival, three months at Kadesh, Aaron's death, the retreat, the return — Seder Olam 9:2 whole (Serah and Jochebed among the comers and the leavers, 10:2)"), ('DATA', "DECISION (4) — THE PLACE AN OPEN ROW (the retelling rul