FACT place_name.the_place_chosen(the_name_pronounced_only_there) = ("the Name pronounced only there (12:5) — the priestly blessing's Name as written in the Temple, by its substitute in the provinces (Mishnah Sotah 7:6; Sotah 38a:10 by analogy; 38a:11 R. Yoshiya's transposition of Exodus 20:20 — OR.altar('every_place') by CALL): the priest who pronounces the Name in the provinces accepted against", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 12:5 — "to put His name there" — the Name\'s placing [\'1Kgs 14:21\', \'2Chr 12:13\', \'Deut 12:5\']; "to make His name dwell there" [\'Deut 12:11\', \'Deut 14:23\', \'Deut 16:11\', \'Deut 16:2\', \'Deut 16:6\', \'Deut 26:2\']; the Name in the chapter 23 bare tokens; Exodus 20:20\'s "in every place where I cause My name to be mentioned" [\'Exod 20:24\'] (the transposition\'s seat)'), ('MOVE', "Mishnah Sotah 7:6 (at 38a:1); Sotah 38a:10, 38a:11 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_ordinances (CALL) — OR.altar(every_place) = hapax_the_name_mentioned — THE NAME PRONOUNCED ONLY THERE — the priestly blessing: in the Temple the Name as written, in the provinces by its substitute (Mishnah Sotah 7:6); 38a:10 by the verbal analogy 'to put His name there' / 'to put My name there' (I2 — checked in MIDDOT.md); 38a:11 R. YOSHIYA'S TRANSPOSITION of Exodus 20:20 — 'in every place where I cause My name to be mentioned I will come to you' read 'in every place where I come to you — the Temple — there you may mention My name': the altar's clause (OR.altar('every_place') the hapax by CALL) read backward; Sotah 38b:10 the do-not-read reading (named, no code)"), ('DATA', "the exam's person the priest who pronounces the Name as written in the provinces — accepted against (the substitute); the transposition named in MIDDOT's entry (no code); Onkelos 12:5 the Shekhinah supplied")])
FACT place_name.the_place_chosen(the_stations_six_rows) = ("the stations' six rows (12:9-11) — the wilderness permitted / forbidden under the Tabernacle, Gilgal permitted, Shiloh forbidden, Nob and Gibeon permitted, Jerusalem forbidden forever (Mishnah Zevachim 14:4-8; Zevachim 112b:9-12): SD.eras('table'), SA.platform('eras') and JO.the_command('private_altar_eras') by CALL agreeing — the table read, unmoved; the one who offers a voluntary offering at Gilgal accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 12:9-11 — "you have not yet come to the rest … when He gives you rest … then the place" — THE STATIONS: the wilderness, Gilgal, Shiloh, Nob and Gibeon, Jerusalem; "the place" in the chapter [3, 5, 11, 14, 18, 21, 26] (the seats of the noun with the article counted)'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_shemini_day (CALL) — SD.eras(table) = ['permitted', 'banned', 'permitted', 'banned', 'permitted', 'banned']; cold_run_sanctions (CALL) — SA.platform(eras) = ['permitted', 'forbidden', 'permitted', 'forbidden', 'permitted', 'forbidden_forever']; cold_run_journeys (CALL) — JO.the_command(private_altar_eras) = the private altar's eras (Mishnah Zevachim 14:4-8); Mishnah Zevachim 14:4-8 with Zevachim 112b:9-12, 118b:13-119a:2 (read whole at the docket) — THE STATIONS' SIX ROWS at their folio (Zevachim 112b:9-12 — Mishnah 14:4-8): before the Tabernacle the high places PERMITTED; the Tabernacle FORBIDDEN; Gilgal PERMITTED; Shiloh FORBIDDEN (the rest); Nob and Gibeon PERMITTED; Jerusalem FORBIDDEN FOREVER (the inheritance) — THE THREE CELLS AGREE (shemini_day's table, sanctions' platform, journeys' private altar eras — read, not written: the chapter's law reads the table and writes no row of it, DD5); THE ERAS' DURATIONS — the wilderness 39, Gilgal 14, Shiloh 369, Nob and Gibeon 57 to the 480th year (118b:13-119a:2 — Seder Olam 11's fourteen at its Bavli seat, the export's chapter EMPTY)"), ('DATA', "the readback rows 12:11 and 12:14 — VERBATIM in kind by CALL (the eras table); THE ERAS TABLE UNMOVED a DATA row (the_eras_table_unmoved — six rows, the platform and the journeys agreeing); the exam's person the one who offers a voluntary offering at Gilgal — the permitted era: accepted")])
FACT place_name.the_place_chosen(the_three_commandments_of_the_entry) = ("the three commandments of the entry (12:10-11) — a king, Amalek, the chosen House, in order (Sanhedrin 20b:8-13 from 12:10-11's 'rest … then the place'); David's rest before the seeking of the site (20b:14; 2 Samuel 7:1): the one who seeks the site before the rest accepted against", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 12:10-11 — "you shall cross the Jordan and dwell in the land … He will give you rest from all your enemies round about … THEN the place which the LORD your God will choose" — the order: the crossing, the rest, the place; "then" [\'Deut 12:11\']; the king unnamed in the chapter (17:14 ahead)'), ('MOVE', "Sanhedrin 20b:8-13, 20b:14 (read whole at the docket); the Sifrei 67:1-3 — THE THREE COMMANDMENTS OF THE ENTRY IN ORDER — to appoint a king, to cut off the seed of Amalek, to build the chosen House (Sanhedrin 20b:8-11; R. Yehuda from 12:10-11's order: the rest from the enemies round about, then the place — 20b:12); DAVID'S REST BEFORE THE SEEKING OF THE SITE — 'when the king dwelt in his house and the LORD had given him rest' (2 Samuel 7:1) then the seeking (20b:14): 12:10-11's order in the run; the Sifrei 67:1-3 the same three"), ('DATA', "the three commandments of the entry a DATA row (the design predicted it — Sanhedrin 20b the exam); the exam's person the one who seeks the site before the rest from the enemies — the order: accepted against (20b:12, 20b:14)")])
DATA KEYS place_name ~ stations|entry|witness: ['the_stations_durations', 'the_three_commandments_of_the_entry']
